These should be added only when they solve observed problems.

---

# 68. Anti-Patterns

Do not:

### Build desktop first and shrink it

Mobile composition should be deliberate.

### Load everything immediately

Especially not Lab and AI infrastructure.

### Optimize only for Lighthouse

Synthetic scores are evidence, not reality.

### Use giant hero videos

Unless the video is central to the project.

### Use animation as identity

The engineering should provide the identity.

### Add a graph library for a simple diagram

Start with HTML/SVG.

### Use tiny technical text

Technical does not mean microscopic.

### Make architecture diagrams visual-only

Provide text.

### Make status color-only

Use labels.

### Hide critical information behind hover

Hover is not universal.

### Use infinite loading

Every asynchronous state needs a resolution.

### Fake progress

Show real progress or indeterminate processing.

### Let an AI API failure break the project page

The demo is subordinate to the website.

### Add dependencies without a measurable reason

Complexity has a cost.

